## Context
Split from 0829 by the TLC sprint lead on 2026-11-09 (verify-gate round 1 on PR #642 ruled
REROLL on this one criterion alone). PR #642 proves by unit tests what goes into
`sudo --preserve-env`; it cannot prove what sudo writes to its journal, which depends on sudoers
settings outside the code and needs a live run on padme with sudo rights.

## Actions
- On padme, run one posture acceptance run (the path that leaked on 2026-11-09 14:05:52).
- Read sudo's journal entry for it (`journalctl`), compare its `ENV=` list with the
  adapters' allowlist (`forwarded_environment`) plus `PATH LANG LC_ALL LC_CTYPE TZ`.
- Record names only, never values, in this ticket's log.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] A posture run's sudo journal line lists only allowlisted names, recorded here (names only)
